    {
      "parameters": {
        "method": "POST",
        "url": "={{ $('Settings').item.json.llmBaseUrl }}/chat/completions",
        "authentication": "genericCredentialType",
        "genericAuthType": "httpHeaderAuth",
        "sendBody": true,
        "specifyBody": "json",
        "jsonBody": "={{ JSON.stringify({ model: $('Settings').item.json.llmModel, temperature: 0.2, response_format: { type: 'json_object' }, messages: [ { role: 'system', content: \"You are the front-desk assistant for \" + $('Settings').item.json.businessName + \", a \" + $('Settings').item.json.businessType + \". Read a website enquiry and return ONLY a JSON object with these keys: category (one of: booking, question, pricing, complaint, urgent, spam, other), urgent (true if the person describes severe pain, an injury that just happened, chest pain, breathing difficulty, heavy bleeding, or anything that sounds like an emergency; otherwise false), summary (one sentence for staff), reply (a warm, short email reply, max 110 words, signed '\" + $('Settings').item.json.signature + \"'). Rules for the reply: use ONLY the facts in BUSINESS INFO; never diagnose or give medical advice; never promise prices, availability or outcomes that are not in BUSINESS INFO; if urgent, tell them to call \" + $('Settings').item.json.emergencyAdvice + \" and do not try to help further; for bookings, share the booking link; if you don't know, say a team member will reply within \" + $('Settings').item.json.responseTime + \". Write in the same language as the enquiry. For spam, reply with an empty string.\\n\\nBUSINESS INFO:\\n\" + $('Settings').item.json.businessInfo + \"\\nBooking link: \" + $('Settings').item.json.bookingLink + \"\" }, { role: 'user', content: 'Name: ' + $json.name + '\\nEmail: ' + $json.email + '\\nPhone: ' + $json.phone + '\\nMessage: ' + $json.message }] }) }}",
        "options": {
          "timeout": 30000
        }
      },
      "id": "b0452b28-fc03-4d1f-afae-ba816d2202ec",
      "name": "AI Triage & Draft",
      "type": "n8n-nodes-base.httpRequest",
      "typeVersion": 4.2,
      "position": [
        1100,
        200
      ],
      "notes": "Any OpenAI-compatible API works (Groq free tier, OpenAI, OpenRouter, a local Ollama at http://localhost:11434/v1). Credential: Header Auth, name 'Authorization', value 'Bearer YOUR_KEY'.",
      "retryOnFail": true,
      "maxTries": 2,
      "onError": "continueRegularOutput"
    },
    {
      "parameters": {
        "jsCode": "// Read the AI's JSON safely; fall back to a polite holding reply if anything is off.\nconst s = $('Settings').first().json;\nconst lead = $('Is Valid?').first().json;\nlet ai = {};\ntry {\n  const content = $json.choices?.[0]?.message?.content ?? '{}';\n  ai = JSON.parse(content.replace(/^```(json)?|```$/g, '').trim());\n} catch (e) { ai = {}; }\nconst allowed = ['booking','question','pricing','complaint','urgent','spam','other'];\nconst category = allowed.includes(ai.category) ? ai.category : 'other';\nconst urgent = ai.urgent === true || category === 'urgent';\nconst fallback = `Hi ${lead.name},\\n\\nThanks for getting in touch with ${s.businessName}. A member of our team will reply within ${s.responseTime}.\\n\\n${s.signature}`;\nconst reply = (typeof ai.reply === 'string' && ai.reply.trim().length > 20) ? ai.reply.trim() : fallback;\nreturn [{ json: {\n  ...lead, category, urgent,\n  summary: String(ai.summary || lead.message.slice(0, 140)),\n  reply: category === 'spam' ? '' : reply,\n  aiOk: Object.keys(ai).length > 0,\n}}];"
      },
